<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hunan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hunan is a province of south-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, lying mostly south of Lake Dongting along the Xiang river, with its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changsha">Changsha</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a> it formed part of the state of Chu, and in the 10th century it was the seat of the independent kingdom of Ma Chu. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rice">rice</a> fields made it a granary of later China, and it was the home province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mao-zedong">Mao Zedong</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hunan.jpg" alt="Hunan" width="320" height="162" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: chensiyuan · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:1_zhangjiajie_huangshizhai_wulingyuan_panorama_2012.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
